    "abstract": "We report the magnetic structure and properties of a thiocyanate-based honeycomb magnet [Na(OH2)3]Mn(NCS)3 which crystallises in the unusual low-symmetry trigonal space group P 3 . Magnetic measurements on powder samples show this material is an antiferromagnet (ordering temperature TN , mag = 18 . 1(6) K) and can be described by nearest neighbour antiferromagnetic interactions J = − 11 . 07(4) K. A method for growing neutron-diffraction sized single crystals (>10 mm3) is demonstrated. Low temperature neutron single crystal diffraction shows that the compound adopts the collinear antiferromagnetic structure with TN , neut = 18 . 94(7) K, magnetic space group P 3̄′ . Low temperature second-harmonic generation (SHG) measurements provide no evidence of breaking of the centre of symmetry.",
